WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.891
Welcome to domain one of the Network Plus N10-009 exam: networking concepts.

00:00:04.891 --> 00:00:10.876
It is worth twenty-three percent of the exam and it is the foundation for every other domain.

00:00:10.876 --> 00:00:20.979
We will move quickly through the O S I model, appliances, cloud, ports and protocols, cabling, topologies, I P v four addressing, and modern network designs.

00:00:21.679 --> 00:00:23.880
The O S I model has seven layers.

00:00:23.880 --> 00:00:28.148
Layer seven, application, provides network services to programs.

00:00:28.148 --> 00:00:32.016
Six, presentation, formats, encrypts, and compresses data.

00:00:32.016 --> 00:00:35.417
Five, session, sets up, manages, and ends sessions.

00:00:35.417 --> 00:00:40.552
Four, transport, handles end-to-end delivery and ports, with T C P and U D P.

00:00:40.552 --> 00:00:46.687
Three, network, handles logical addressing and routing, which is where I P and routers live.

00:00:46.687 --> 00:00:51.755
Two, data link, uses frames and mac addresses, which is where switches live.

00:00:51.755 --> 00:00:54.956
And one, physical, moves bits across the medium.

00:00:54.956 --> 00:01:00.491
A classic memory aid is: Please Do Not Throw Sausage Pizza Away, from layer one up.

00:01:01.191 --> 00:01:03.681
Objective one point two covers appliances.

00:01:03.681 --> 00:01:07.119
A router forwards packets between networks at layer three.

00:01:07.119 --> 00:01:13.580
A switch forwards frames by mac address at layer two, and a layer three switch can also route between V LANs.

00:01:13.580 --> 00:01:18.263
A firewall filters traffic with rules, and a stateful firewall tracks sessions.

00:01:18.263 --> 00:01:22.413
An I D S detects attacks, while an I P S sits in line and blocks them.

00:01:22.413 --> 00:01:33.142
A load balancer spreads requests across servers, a proxy stands in for clients or servers and can filter content, and an access point connects wireless clients to the wired network.

00:01:33.842 --> 00:01:38.434
For cloud, know the deployment models: public, private, hybrid, and community.

00:01:38.434 --> 00:01:41.318
Know the service models, I a a S, pass, and sass.

00:01:41.318 --> 00:01:46.617
You manage less at each step, with I a a S giving you the most control and sass the least.

00:01:46.617 --> 00:01:50.090
A V P C is your own isolated network inside a public cloud.

00:01:50.090 --> 00:01:56.625
You connect to it with a V P N over the internet, or with a private direct connection that avoids the internet.

00:01:56.625 --> 00:02:04.690
Security groups and network A C Ls control traffic in the cloud, and network functions virtualization runs network functions as software.

00:02:05.390 --> 00:02:11.729
Objective one point four is ports and protocols, and the exam expects you to know them cold.

00:02:11.729 --> 00:02:14.004
F T P uses twenty and twenty-one.

00:02:14.004 --> 00:02:16.278
S S H and S F T P use twenty-two.

00:02:16.278 --> 00:02:17.863
Telnet is twenty-three.

00:02:17.863 --> 00:02:19.447
S M T P is twenty-five.

00:02:19.447 --> 00:02:20.895
D N S is fifty-three.

00:02:20.895 --> 00:02:23.720
D H C P uses sixty-seven and sixty-eight.

00:02:23.720 --> 00:02:25.236
T F T P is sixty-nine.

00:02:25.236 --> 00:02:28.819
H T T P is eighty and H T T P S is four forty-three.

00:02:28.819 --> 00:02:32.403
P O P three is one-ten and I map is one forty-three.

00:02:32.403 --> 00:02:34.194
N T P is one twenty-three.

00:02:34.194 --> 00:02:38.811
S N M P uses one sixty-one for polling and one sixty-two for traps.

00:02:38.811 --> 00:02:43.015
L D A P is three eighty-nine and L D A P S is six thirty-six.

00:02:43.015 --> 00:02:49.148
S M B is four forty-five, syslog is five fourteen, and R D P is thirty-three eighty-nine.

00:02:49.848 --> 00:02:51.299
Know the traffic types.

00:02:51.299 --> 00:02:54.138
Unicast goes from one sender to one receiver.

00:02:54.138 --> 00:02:55.778
Multicast goes to a group.

00:02:55.778 --> 00:02:58.428
Broadcast goes to everyone on the segment.

00:02:58.428 --> 00:03:04.233
And anycast uses one address that is shared by several servers, and the nearest one answers.

00:03:04.233 --> 00:03:09.091
T C P is connection-oriented and reliable, and it uses a three-way handshake.

00:03:09.091 --> 00:03:16.284
U D P is connectionless and fast, but it does not guarantee delivery, which suits voice, video, and D N S queries.

00:03:16.984 --> 00:03:21.236
For cabling, Cat five E carries one gigabit over one hundred meters.

00:03:21.236 --> 00:03:28.865
Cat six carries ten gigabits up to fifty-five meters, and Cat six A carries ten gigabits over the full one hundred meters.

00:03:28.865 --> 00:03:37.870
Multimode fiber is used over shorter distances with cheaper optics, and single-mode fiber reaches the longest distances, measured in kilometers.

00:03:37.870 --> 00:03:44.374
Transceivers plug into switches: S F P is one gigabit, S F P plus is ten gigabits, and Q S F P is forty.

00:03:44.374 --> 00:03:48.876
A D A C or Twinax cable is a short copper link, typically inside a rack.

00:03:49.576 --> 00:03:50.229
Topologies.

00:03:50.229 --> 00:03:53.373
In a star, every device connects to a central switch.

00:03:53.373 --> 00:03:58.297
In a mesh, nodes connect to each other, fully or partially, which gives redundancy.

00:03:58.297 --> 00:04:01.263
Hub and spoke connects branches to a central site.

00:04:01.263 --> 00:04:09.094
For campus designs, know the three-tier model: core, distribution, and access, and the collapsed core, which combines the first two.

00:04:09.094 --> 00:04:13.900
Data centers use spine and leaf, where every leaf switch connects to every spine.

00:04:13.900 --> 00:04:20.366
There, traffic between servers is called east-west, and traffic in and out of the data center is north-south.

00:04:21.066 --> 00:04:22.636
Now I P v four addressing.

00:04:22.636 --> 00:04:31.333
The private ranges are ten dot zero slash eight, one seventy-two dot sixteen slash twelve, and one ninety-two dot one sixty-eight slash sixteen.

00:04:31.333 --> 00:04:37.674
The range one sixty-nine dot two fifty-four is A P I P A, which a host uses when it cannot reach D H C P.

00:04:37.674 --> 00:04:40.996
One twenty-seven dot zero dot zero dot one is loopback.

00:04:40.996 --> 00:04:45.827
For subnetting, usable hosts equal two to the power of the host bits, minus two.

00:04:45.827 --> 00:04:49.028
A slash twenty-four has two hundred fifty-four hosts.

00:04:49.028 --> 00:04:56.638
A slash twenty-six has sixty-two hosts, with the mask two fifty-five dot two fifty-five dot two fifty-five dot one ninety-two.

00:04:56.638 --> 00:04:59.054
Practice these until they are automatic.

00:04:59.754 --> 00:05:01.206
Finally, modern designs.

00:05:01.206 --> 00:05:08.530
Software-defined networking separates the control plane from the data plane, so a controller decides and devices forward.

00:05:08.530 --> 00:05:11.798
S D wan manages wide area links centrally with policy.

00:05:11.798 --> 00:05:15.490
V X LAN carries layer two traffic over a layer three network.

00:05:15.490 --> 00:05:19.485
Zero trust means verify every request and never trust by location.

00:05:19.485 --> 00:05:23.116
Sassy delivers network and security services from the cloud.

00:05:23.116 --> 00:05:26.929
Infrastructure as code configures devices from versioned files.

00:05:26.929 --> 00:05:35.826
And I P version six uses one hundred twenty-eight bit addresses, with dual stack, tunneling, or nat sixty-four to transition from I P version four.

00:05:36.526 --> 00:05:40.568
To recap domain one: know all seven layers and what lives at each.

00:05:40.568 --> 00:05:43.875
Memorize the port list, including the secure versions.

00:05:43.875 --> 00:05:47.243
Match cable and transceiver type to speed and distance.

00:05:47.243 --> 00:05:50.121
Know the three-tier and spine-and-leaf designs.

00:05:50.121 --> 00:05:51.959
And be able to subnet quickly.

00:05:51.959 --> 00:05:52.571
Good luck.
